The Buddy-derived source, tests, and fixtures have been modified for Jolt in
2026. Modifications include namespace mapping to jolt.crypto, replacement of
JVM/Bouncy Castle/Apache Commons mechanics with Jolt and OpenSSL facilities,
and additional behavioral regression tests. Prominent modification notices are
also retained in the derived source and test files. The applicable Apache
License 2.0 text is provided in LICENSE-buddy-core.

The jolt.crypto.util.ecdsa portion of this port is derived from the ECDSA
implementation in Nimbus JOSE + JWT, as included by Buddy Core.

